Task 1 — Part of #1041 (product): withdraw a dead MCP server's tools.
• Problem: if a stdio MCP server crashes mid-session, its tools stay listed and the model keeps calling a server that's gone. yoagent 0.25.15, already in our lockfile, can now notice the exit and withdraw them through McpToolSource.
• Change: both connect paths (normal and prefixed) go through one function in src/mcp_prefix.rs that installs McpToolSource. The edit in src/agent_builder.rs is kept to a call swap because that file is 14 lines under its size cap.
• Side effect the task warns about: a failed connect no longer throws away the servers that already connected. A source test that counts exact rebuild sites will fail until its counts are updated, and the task says to update them on purpose with a reason.
• Test: a small sh stub MCP server that we start, kill, then check its tool is gone, plus a case where a live server keeps its tool.
• Left for later: telling the user and the model why the tools vanished. The task posts that on #1041 before pushing.

Task 2 — Part of #1071 (evolve): stop the `test-model` records at their source.
• Problem: @yuanhao did his half of #1071 this morning. But the first synthesize spend row has 4 test-model records mixed in with the 3 real ones, and the report would show them as 4 uncosted calls.
• Change: first read those records in full and try to reproduce with YOYO_AUDIT=1 cargo test. Then fix the writer and pin it with a test, plus a check that a real audited run still writes its record. If it doesn't reproduce, the task reports that on #1071 instead of shipping a guessed fix.
• Not touched: adding "synthesize" to PHASE_SPEND_PHASES waits until next session, once there's a clean row. I told him in the thread I wouldn't land that while it counts test records.

